<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-17">17 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Traditional date of the death of Saint Patrick</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition Patrick, the Romano-British missionary to Ireland, died on 17 March, though the year is uncertain. His feast became Ireland's national day, celebrated by the Irish diaspora worldwide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-7">7 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Western Emperor Majorian is executed on Ricimer's orders</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Majorian, the last Western emperor to attempt a real recovery of the empire, was arrested and beheaded by his general Ricimer. Afterwards Ricimer ruled through puppet emperors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-19">19 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Libius Severus is proclaimed Western Roman emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Libius Severus, a native of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucania">Lucania</a>, became Western Roman emperor after the general Ricimer overthrew his predecessor Majorian. He was the first of a series of emperors highly dependent on Ricimer, who is often presumed to have held most real power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
